# Intentional divergence from lib/slop-env/defaults/CLAUDE.md (ADR-0015).
#
# This template's CLAUDE.md carries a "## Worktrees" section documenting how
# worktrunk (`wt`) behaves inside the jail: worktrees are placed under
# .git/slop-worktrees/ (set via WORKTRUNK_WORKTREE_PATH) so they stay reachable
# in the cwd-only jail and out of `git status`. That guidance belongs here
# because the claude-code template ships `wt` (projectPkgs) AND the worktrunk /
# wt-switch-create skills.
#
# The lib default is the zero-touch / apps baseline. It ships NEITHER the `wt`
# binary (worktrunk lives only in template projectPkgs) NOR the skills, so
# documenting worktrunk there would point the agent at tooling it doesn't have.
# The WORKTRUNK_WORKTREE_PATH env var the library sets is harmless there —
# nothing reads it without `wt`.
#
# This marker disables the template-default-config-matches-lib drift ratchet for
# this whole config dir. The ONLY intended divergence is the "## Worktrees"
# section. Keep everything else in CLAUDE.md — and all of rules/ — in sync with
# lib/slop-env/defaults/ by hand.
